WEBVTT

NOTE Ruwaidix source-grounded narration; original owner archive and labeled explanations.

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.753
An airway can reopen and still be injured. As an air

00:00:04.753 --> 00:00:05.241
bubble

00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:08.651
advances through liquid, it leaves a moving boundary

00:00:08.651 --> 00:00:09.176
that the

00:00:09.176 --> 00:00:11.143
epithelial cells cannot simply ignore.

00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:17.974
The question in our experiments was physical before it

00:00:17.974 --> 00:00:18.184
was

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.302
pharmacological. Could the passage of that interface

00:00:21.302 --> 00:00:21.782
damage a

00:00:21.782 --> 00:00:25.135
cultured monolayer, even without the full complexity

00:00:25.135 --> 00:00:25.780
of a lung?

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:32.674
We worked with L2 alveolar epithelial cells in a

00:00:32.674 --> 00:00:33.728
parallel-plate

00:00:33.728 --> 00:00:38.005
flow chamber. The chamber let us expose cells to a

00:00:38.005 --> 00:00:38.860
controlled

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.260
advancing air–liquid interface.

00:00:43.437 --> 00:00:46.744
After exposure, fluorescent viability staining helped

00:00:46.744 --> 00:00:47.243
us count

00:00:47.243 --> 00:00:51.454
damaged cells. Images of the cytoskeleton gave another

00:00:51.454 --> 00:00:52.000
view of

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.330
how cells responded to the mechanical event.

00:00:58.603 --> 00:01:01.232
Those colored fields were measurements, not

00:01:01.232 --> 00:01:02.393
illustrations of an

00:01:02.393 --> 00:01:05.869
entire organ. A signal could document injury without

00:01:05.869 --> 00:01:06.604
telling us,

00:01:06.604 --> 00:01:09.973
on its own, which molecular mechanism caused it.

00:01:13.103 --> 00:01:16.610
We also investigated whether changing the cells before

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:17.129
exposure

00:01:17.129 --> 00:01:21.005
could alter their susceptibility. That was a test of

00:01:21.005 --> 00:01:21.601
response

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:24.968
under specified conditions, not a claim that a

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:25.627
treatment

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:26.521
protects patients.

00:01:30.062 --> 00:01:33.152
Making a result reproducible meant keeping the

00:01:33.152 --> 00:01:34.227
chamber, timing,

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:37.787
controls, and image analysis intelligible. The harder

00:01:37.787 --> 00:01:38.392
part came

00:01:38.392 --> 00:01:41.830
afterward: deciding what those measurements actually

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.020
allowed us to say.

00:01:46.478 --> 00:01:49.515
An airway reopening looks like recovery from a

00:01:49.515 --> 00:01:50.637
distance. At cell

00:01:50.637 --> 00:01:53.473
scale, it can be another mechanical challenge. Our

00:01:53.473 --> 00:01:54.040
experiment

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:57.443
gives that hidden event a way to be studied.
